    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d734-a3">

                <pb facs="1170" n="1074" sameAs="frus:frus1874/pg1074"/>

                <opener><seg rendition="#center">[Inclosure 3 in No. 5.]</seg></opener>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">Mr. Young to Mr.
                            Nunes.</hi></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1873-11-06T22:00:00-05:07">10 <hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >p.m.</hi>
                            <hi rendition="#italic">November</hi> 6,
                    1873</date>.</dateline></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir</hi>: With reference to the reported capture of
                    the steanship Virginius the governor desires me to acquaint you that he has
                    caused the following message to be sent to the British consul at Santiago de
                    Cuba:</p>
                <p>“Governor of Jamaica does not believe, unless judicial condemnation has taken <pb
                        facs="1171" n="1075" xml:id="pg1075"/> place, that Virginius is a pirate. If
                    not a pirate the shooting of any British subjects for being on board cannot be
                    lawful. British subjects may have been shipped here as crew or passengers, and,
                    as Virginius was not armed, and carried from Jamaica no warlike munitions, they
                    may have been ignorant that the vessel was not peacefully bound for Limon Bay,
                    for which port she cleared. Governor suggests a strong demand for suspension of
                    execution at least, pending a formal trial, in the case of all who claim to be
                    British subjects.”</p>
                <p>I have the honor, &amp;c,</p>
                <closer><signed>WILLIAM A. S. YOUNG.</signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
